# Line endings — sim_portability.md P-4.
#
# Every text file in this module is LF in the repository AND LF in the working
# tree, on Windows and on Linux alike. Without this, a global `core.autocrlf`
# checks these files out as CRLF on Windows, and then:
#
#   - a committed log under docs/py/logs/ differs between a Windows and a Linux
#     checkout by line ending alone, so the "committed output is the proof"
#     discipline compares two different files;
#   - a golden fixture regenerated on the other platform shows a whole-file
#     diff, which trains people to ignore golden diffs;
#   - bundle.sha256 (R-SIM-3a) would be platform-dependent, which is worse than
#     not having a hash at all.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit and checks out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.mcap  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pdf   binary
